  "source_findings": [
    "Nominal actual voting multiplier is 0.5 SE, while reported intervals use 1.96 SE; dataclass defaults/comments do not select actual settings.",
    "Nominal middle epoch uses CS60-69; new/improved/WIP use CS40-69, assuming the configured CS5-94 schedule. All use Pre5-14 and LateTest85-94.",
    "WIP display key middle markers use Late Train + Early Test although its feature construction includes Train6-9 too.",
    "WIP phi-direction scores, joint statistic threshold and empirical tail rank are distinct outputs; actual label is T above quantile and all direction votes.",
    "Legacy heatmap grids load pre-existing images, identify fish using the first two filename tokens, crop 2% and only iterate classified fish.",
    "Grouping grid splits included/discarded fish, but its pooled numerical rows are not equivalently filtered; normalized-vigor uses a later ANY-block rule.",
    "Legacy scaled heatmaps use bout-mean replacement, per-trial baseline quantile scaling and clipping; this does not equal the classifier outcome transformation.",
    "Legacy scalar grids overlay a cumulative two-feature BLUP schematic on an independently scaled secondary axis; it is not a fitted trial-by-trial trajectory.",
    "The supported isolated worker disables legacy heatmap-grid output even when other individual figure flags are enabled.",
    "Source code supports raw/scaled heatmap grids; the checked archive inventories and scanned mounted roots did not yield their saved Heatmap_Grid files. Combined scalar-grid artifacts were found, hash-verified and inspected.",
